, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet/Portion/Kind-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tuplet-type type indicates the graphical note type of the notes for this portion of the tuplet."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet\/portion\/kind-swift.struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTuplet.Portion.Kind","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTuplet\/Portion\/Kind-swift.struct","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuplet element is present when a tuplet is to be displayed graphically, in addition to the sound data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provided by the time-modification elements. The number attribute is used to distinguish nested tuplets. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bracket attribute is used to indicate the presence of a bracket. If unspecified, the results are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implementation-dependent. The line-shape attribute is used to specify whether the bracket is straight or in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the older curved or slurred style. It is straight by default."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTuplet"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTuplet","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTuplet"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTuplet","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNoteKindValue":{"title":"MXLNoteKindValue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotekindvalue","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteKindValue","abstract":[{"text":"The note-type-value type is used for the MusicXML type element and represents the graphic note type, from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1024th (shortest) to maxima (longest).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet/Portion":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLTuplet.Portion","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTuplet\/Portion","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tuplet-portion type provides optional full control over tuplet specifications. It allows the number and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"note type (including dots) to be set for the actual and normal portions of a single tuplet. If any of these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements are absent, their values are based on the time-modification element."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Portion"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Portion"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet\/portion"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet/Portion/Kind-swift.struct/init(value:font:color:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"MXLTuplet.Portion.Kind","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet\/portion\/kind-swift.struct\/init(value:font:color:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"font"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","text":"MXLFont"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"init(value:font:color:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTuplet\/Portion\/Kind-swift.struct\/init(value:font:color:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"}}}